emoved","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:5101404eb4ea56441031931264ebf6d2c76043351b1ae933756a4f85f52d552f","file":"preprints/The-free-energy-of-the-Ising-random-perceptron-September-24-2026/build/sections/model.tex","line":88,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"5656beee0d64c5d053fe8f9d098e8af1cd74da08f1b7578d80f2948dc2e7453a","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-free-energy-of-the-Ising-random-perceptron-September-24-2026/build/sections/model.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:5101404eb4ea56441031931264ebf6d2c76043351b1ae933756a4f85f52d552f","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-free-energy-of-the-Ising-random-perceptron-September-24-2026/build/sections/model.tex#L88"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every $\\alpha>0$ and every bounded Borel $f:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{thm:formula}\n \\lim_{N\\to\\infty}\\mathbb E p_N(f)\n =\\mathcal P_f(\\alpha)\n :=\\inf_{q\\in\\mathcal Q}\\{\\alpha V_f(q)+S_{\\mathrm I}(q)\\}.\n\\end{equation}\nMoreover, $p_N(f)$ converges to $\\mathcal P_f(\\alpha)$ in probability.\nThe variational value is finite. In particular, the conclusion holds for\n$f=\\beta\\phi$ at every $\\beta>0$ and every bounded continuous activation\n$\\phi$, without symmetry, concavity, or a smallness restriction."}
